ia","wikipediaTitle":"Juche Tower","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Juche-Tower-2014.jpg/1280px-Juche-Tower-2014.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Juche-Tower-2014.jpg/500px-Juche-Tower-2014.jpg","w":1200,"h":1721,"author":"Bjørn Christian Tørrissen","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juche-Tower-2014.jpg"}},{"id":"pyongyang_arch_of_reunification","areaId":"pyongyang","name":"Arch of Reunification","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":38.96453,"lng":125.71582},"visitMinutes":30,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"pyongyang_arch_of_reunification","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":51,"commonsNearby":6,"wikiPageviews":5226,"wikidataSitelinks":29,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-19"},"hashtags":["archofreunification","pyongyang"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"The Arch of Reunification, officially the Monument to the Three-Point Charter for National Reunification, was a sculptural arch located south of Pyongyang, the capital of North Korea. It was opened in August 2001 to commemorate Korean reunification proposals put forward by Kim Il Sung.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Arch of Reunification","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Monument-to-National-Reunification-2014.jpg/1280px-Monument-to-National-Reunification-2014.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Monument-to-National-Reunification-2014.jpg/500px-Monument-to-National-Reunification-2014.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Bjørn Christian Tørrissen","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monument-to-National-Reunification-2014.jpg"}},{"id":"pyongyang_arch_of_triumph","areaId":"pyongyang","name":"Arch of Triumph","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":39.04465,"lng":125.7531},"visitMinutes":30,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"pyongyang_arch_of_triumph","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":4,"commonsNearby":75,"wikiPageviews":3722,"wikidataSitelinks":32,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-19"},"hashtags":["archoftriumph","pyongyang"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"The Arch of Triumph is a triumphal arch in Pyongyang, North Korea. It was built to commemorate the Korean resistance to Japan from 1925 to 1945. It is the second tallest memorial arch in the world, after Monumento a la Revolución in Mexico, standing 60 m (197 ft) high and 50 m (164 ft) wide.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Arch of Triumph (Pyongyang)","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/0656_-_Nordkorea_2015_-_Pj%C3%B6ngjang_-_Triumphbogen_%2822347022434%29.jpg/1280px-0656_-_Nordkorea_2015_-_Pj%C3%B6ngjang_-_Triumphbogen_%2822347022434%29.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/0656_-_Nordkorea_2015_-_Pj%C3%B6ngjang_-_Triumphbogen_%2822347022434%29.jpg/500px-0656_-_Nordkorea_2015_-_Pj%C3%B6ngjang_-_Triumphbogen_%2822347022434%29.jpg","w":1200,"h":778,"author":"Uwe Brodrecht","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:0656_-_Nordkorea_2015_-_Pj%C3%B6ngjang_-_Triumphbogen_(22347022434).jpg"}},{"id":"pyongyang_yanggakdo_international_hotel","areaId":"pyongyang","name":"Yanggakdo International Hotel","category":"landmark","tags":["views","photo"],"location":{"lat":38.99893,"lng":125.75115},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"pyongyang_yanggakdo_international_hotel","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://www.cooks.org.kp/kp/index.php/first/restaurants/14","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":4,"commonsNearby":110,"wikiPageviews":2910,"wikidataSitelinks":22,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-19"},"hashtags":["yanggakdointernationalhotel","pyongyang"],"hours"